WEBVTT

00:08:57.855 --> 00:09:01.288
CA: So really, both Linux
and Git kind of arose

00:09:01.312 --> 00:09:03.648
almost as an unintended consequence

00:09:03.672 --> 00:09:06.343
of your desire not to have
to work with too many people.

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:07.518
LT: Absolutely. Yes.

00:09:07.542 --> 00:09:08.622
(Laughter)

00:09:08.646 --> 00:09:10.296
CA: That's amazing.
LT: Yeah.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.812
(Applause)

00:09:11.836 --> 00:09:15.227
And yet, you're the man
who's transformed technology

00:09:15.251 --> 00:09:16.568
not just once but twice,

00:09:16.592 --> 00:09:19.175
and we have to try
and understand why it is.

00:09:19.199 --> 00:09:20.883
You've given us some clues, but ...

00:09:20.907 --> 00:09:25.548
Here's a picture of you as a kid,
with a Rubik's Cube.

00:09:25.572 --> 00:09:29.692
You mentioned that you've been
programming since you were like 10 or 11,

00:09:29.716 --> 00:09:31.081
half your life.